  <prompt>Make the customer's containers fit what unified-access-control-r2 builds: secure records get their own containers at runtime, and a record that is not secure stores its files in its business unit's container.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Dataverse Web API, SPE, PowerShell provisioning scripts).</role>

  <goal>
    H8 creates exactly ONE container per customer — the ROOT container (the root business unit's; the default, email and
    communication-archive container). Other containers are created by the BFF at runtime and are not provisioning's: one per
    secure project / matter / work assignment (ProvisionProjectEndpoint → ContainerOperations.CreateContainerAsync, bound to
    the record's business unit and marked), and any further business-unit container through the SPE admin plane (bound and
    marked). uac-r2 task 076 resolves a record that is NOT secure to its owning business unit's `sprk_containerid`; the
    legacy Provision-Customer.ps1 step 10 wrote that column on the root unit, but L2 never did — so on a fresh Model 1 stamp
    every non-secure record resolved to no container. (1) H7 links the root business unit to H8's container. (2) Every
    container a script creates carries the `spaarkeCustomerId` marker the BFF requires (T227d), as BFF and H8 containers do.
    (3) The wording says "one ROOT container per customer" and names the runtime containers. (4) The provisioning runbook
    and skill require the secure-record environment setup uac-r2 documents (Secure Record business unit, named owner
    team, Secure Record Owner role, sprk_issecure field security), gated by that guide's own verification checklist.
  </goal>

  <context>
