  <constraints>
    <constraint source="data">Never overwrite a root business unit's non-empty `sprk_containerid` that names another container: Resumable, naming both, nothing written (it would move the customer's non-secure files).</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Real HTTP against a hand-written HttpMessageHandler fake — never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Do not change uac-r2's resolver or the secure-record setup scripts; the runbook points at uac-r2's guide (one source), it does not copy its steps.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">H7 writer: root-business-unit link after the env-var values (same token); typed failures; handler maps them; tests.</step>
    <step order="2">Scripts: the marker in the PowerShell bind helper and its three callers; ArchTest parity + every call passes -CustomerId.</step>
    <step order="3">Wording + runbook/skill secure-record setup phase; verify; Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Root unit empty → PATCH then read back; equal → no write; another container → Resumable `root-business-unit-container-conflict` naming both, no PATCH; no root / two roots → Resumable `root-business-unit-unresolved`; a read-back mismatch fails (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H7 passes H8's container as the link target (handler test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests: the PowerShell marker constant equals the C# one and appears in one script; every Invoke-SpeContainerBindOrRemove call passes -CustomerId (with a seeded negative control).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No living doc says "one container per customer" without "root"; the inventory lists the runtime containers with both custom properties.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests pass.</criterion>
