  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (SESSION 39). Owner question: "one container per customer, ever — but what about the Secure Record
    container?" Answer: aligned in design — H8 makes ONE ROOT container; uac-r2 gives every secure project / matter / work
    assignment its own container at runtime (ProvisionProjectEndpoint → ContainerOperations.CreateContainerAsync: bound to
    the record's business unit, then marked spaarkeCustomerId); the Secure Record business unit itself has no container.
    Three real gaps were found and closed:
    - H7 now links the root business unit to H8's container (businessunit.sprk_containerid): equal → no write; empty →
      PATCH + read back; another container → Resumable root-business-unit-container-conflict naming both, nothing written;
      0/2 roots → Resumable root-business-unit-unresolved. uac-r2 task 076 resolves a non-secure record to its owning
      unit's container; legacy Provision-Customer.ps1 step 10 wrote it, L2 never did — a fresh stamp would have stored no
      non-secure file. The link runs BEFORE the values (deviation from step 1's "after": a conflict then writes nothing).
      configVer carries a link version, so an H7 completed before the link existed does not short-circuit past it.
    - Script-created containers carry the marker: Invoke-SpeContainerBindOrRemove takes -CustomerId (= the BFF's
      Customer__Id, ordinal), writes + reads back both properties, removes the container if either did not land;
      New-BusinessUnitContainer / Provision-Customer step 10 / Create-NewContainerType pass it. ArchTest
      SpeContainerMarkerParityTests: one PS constant equal to the C# contract; every bind call passes -CustomerId (seeded
      negative control).
    - Secure-record environment setup (Secure Record BU, named owner team, role, depth, sprk_issecure FLS) is in no handler:
      deployment guide §7.11 + provision-environment Step 6d now require uac-r2's SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md, gated by
      its §7 checklist (one source — not copied).
    - Wording: "one ROOT container per customer" in constraints, guide §7.5, topology doc, inventory (+ rows for secure-record
      and further business-unit containers), write-path registry I-4, L2 comments. Kept deliberately: the catalog note in
      manifest.yaml (editing it changes generated output) and a BFF comment in SpeAdminTenantScope (about config isolation;
      not worth a BFF touch).
    - Read-only live check: spaarke-bff-dev has Customer__Id = spaarke (secure containers created there are marked).
      uac-r2's branch (87 commits ahead of master) changes no container-creation code.
    - Step 9.5: adr-check 0 violations / 5 warnings (W1 configVer, W4 doc, W5 two doc sites — fixed; W2/W3 hand-written
      HttpMessageHandler under the project's test folder = existing project convention). code-review 0 critical; fixed F4,
      F5 (PATCH 403, read-back failure, timeout, cancellation tests), F9-F12; F3 recorded above; F6/F7/F8/F13 accepted
      (timeout handling differs from the older UpsertOneAsync; no If-Match on a single-writer step; label cosmetic; regex
      limits documented by the negative control). F1 → T186 live unknown: the BFF app registration (H7's identity, before
      H10) can write businessunit. F2: no L2-provisioned stamp exists yet (T186 is the first live run), so nothing to backfill.
    - Tests: ControlPlane 2191 (2189 + 2) / 0 failed; ArchTests 831/831; Worker build 0 warnings. No BFF code changed (no
      publish-size measurement needed).
  </notes>
